  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: We are currently sitting under an upper\nlevel ridge centered over the Pacific, which will prevent us from\nseeing any active weather. As a result we will see high \ntemperatures begin to slowly climb throughout the week, with highs\nin the upper 50s/low 60s. Overnight lows will remain in the mid \nto low 30s, with some spots in higher elevations seeing lows in \nthe upper 20s. The northernmost portions of the forecast area may \nsee elevated wind gusts, up to 15-25 mph, in the afternoons of \nSunday and Monday due to the passage of a few embedded shortwave \ntroughs. \n\nBeginning next Saturday, model guidance suggests the passage of \nan upper level trough as well as a potential atmospheric river \nevent. With this brings the possibility of rain and snow showers \nnext weekend. Due to this event being so far out, there is low\nconfidence on the occurrence of it as well as any associated\nimpacts.  \n\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: There is high confidence in the\nridge building throughout the week, bringing rising temperatures\nand calm weather. There is low confidence on the upper level\ntrough next weekend and any impacts it may have.",
